{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
On the morning of the third day thunder [Ab]rolled across the [Eb]plain
Lightning on the mountain and a [Ab]cloud as dark as [Bb]rain
The [Eb]horn blew loud and louder and the camp [Ab]began to [Eb]shake
Sinai wrapped in smoke and fire [Bb]for the people's [Eb]sake
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I am [Bb]the LORD your [Cm]God
Who brought you [Ab]out of the land of E[Eb]gypt
Out of the [Bb]house of slave[Cm]ry
You shall [Ab]have no other [Bb]gods before [Eb]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
You shall not make for your[Ab]self an i[Eb]dol
You shall not misuse the name [Ab]of the LORD your [Bb]God
Re[Eb]member the Sabbath day by [Ab]keeping it [Eb]holy
Six days you shall [Bb]labor and do all your [Eb]work
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Cm]Honor your father and your [Ab]mother
You [Eb]shall not murder
You shall not commit adultery
[Ab]You shall not [Bb]steal
You [Eb]shall not give false testimony [Ab]against your [Eb]neighbor
You shall not [Bb]covet your neighbor's [Eb]house
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Not [Cm]a burden laid on slaves but a [Ab]road for people [Eb]free
Ten words spoken from the fire for all [Ab]who would be[Bb]lieve
[Eb]Showing steadfast love to a [Ab]thousand genera[Eb]tions
Of those who [Bb]love me and keep my com[Eb]mandments
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

